{
  "enabled": false,
  "name": "Feature flag audit",
  "description": "Manual-trigger audit of every feature flag in a project (active and archived). Identifies cleanup candidates using metadata returned by the Unleash MCP server. Enable when you want the trigger button to appear in the Hooks panel.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Run a feature flag audit using the Unleash MCP server. Steps: (1) Use the project the user names; if they name none, call search (kind: projects) and ask which one. (2) Call search (kind: flags) with that project and stages set to define, develop, production, cleanup and archived — archived flags only come back when that stage is listed. Page with offset and limit until you reach total. (3) Skip flags whose type is kill-switch or permission — these are permanent by Unleash's defaults. (4) For each remaining flag, call inspect (kind: flag) for its details, including when SDKs last saw it in each environment. (5) Evaluate these signals in order: (a) staleness is stale or potentially_stale → include in report; (b) lifecycle stage is archived → already archived in Unleash but code references may remain, include for code cleanup; (c) SDKs last saw it more than 30 days ago in every environment where it is enabled → no SDK has hit it, include; (d) age since creation > expected lifetime for its type (check steering/cleanup-cadence.md) → overdue, include. (6) Produce a prioritized cleanup report sorted by: stale flags first, then archived flags, then by oldest last-seen time across enabled environments, then by how far past its expected lifetime. For each candidate, include: flag name, type, lifecycle stage, age in days, oldest last-seen time, which signals fired, and suggested next action (e.g., 'remove code references, then manage_flag complete', 'archive in Unleash', 'check with feature owner'). (7) Do NOT change anything — no manage_flag or release calls, no code edits. The report is for the user to triage. (8) If inspect returns no last-seen data for some flags, note that in the report rather than guessing."
  }
}
